                                           skos:prefLabel "Multiferroic"@en ;
                                           :elucidation "Materials that exhibit more than one primary ferroic property simultaneously (e.g., coupled ferroelectricity and ferromagnetism), enabling cross-domain field control."@en .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_1d0064d2_d77e_4ec7_b74a_00f98616156f
:EMMO_1d0064d2_d77e_4ec7_b74a_00f98616156f rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                           rdfs:subClassOf :EMMO_8820f251_ad36_43f4_a693_c0e86a89cc1f ;
                                           skos:prefLabel "FunctionalMaterial"@en ;
                                           :elucidation "A functional material is any material that exhibits distinct, reproducible changes in its electronic, magnetic, optical, chemical, or thermal properties when exposed to an external field or environmental change."@en ;
                                           :note "Materials categorised for what they do rather than what they hold up. They are designed to react to their environment, convert energy, or process information."@en .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_1ef0d75a_92c1_466e_9ad9_4bff50a54695
