###  https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_b9695e87_8261_412e_83cd_a86459426a28
:EMMO_b9695e87_8261_412e_83cd_a86459426a28 rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                           rdfs:subClassOf :EMMO_8b0923ab_b500_477b_9ce9_8b3a3e4dc4f2 ;
                                           skos:prefLabel "StateOfMatter"@en ;
                                           :OWLRL2DLAxioms "Disjoint Union Of: CondensedMatter, UncondensedMatter" ,
                                                           "Disjoint Union Of: Gas, Plasma, Liquid, Solid" ;
                                           :elucidation "A superclass made as the disjoint union of all the form under which matter can exist."@en ;
                                           :note "Besides the classical four state, IUPAC Goldbook introduces another categorisation dimension with the distinction between amorphous and crystalline state. A substance can then be the combination of these different categorisation schemes, such as liquid crystal or amorphous solid. However, between crystalline and amorphous states there may be intermediate state called semicrystalline materials where amorphous and crystalline phases are mixed."@en ,
                                                 "Besides the classical four states,we have also the categorisation widely used in material science between condensed (liquid and solid) and uncondensed (gas and plasma) matter."@en ,
                                                 "In physics, a state of matter is one of the distinct forms in which matter can exist. Four states of matter are observable in everyday life: solid, liquid, gas, and plasma."@en ;
                                           :wikipediaReference "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/State_of_matter"@en .


